#
# Behaviour (REFACTOR-MCP §4.3):
#   * Both registerOAuthRoutes(app) (legacy SQLite path) AND
#     registerIdentityPlatformRoutes(app) (new Firebase path) are mounted.
#   * Order: Identity Platform middleware runs first (it owns /mcp). Legacy
#     routes only own the /oauth/* + /.well-known/oauth-* paths and only
#     respond to clients that still possess a SQLite-issued token.
#   * The new flag MCP_AUTH_MODE controls which path is active:
#       MCP_AUTH_MODE=legacy        — only SQLite routes (pre-cutover)
#       MCP_AUTH_MODE=dual          — both (T+0 to T+7)            ← default
#       MCP_AUTH_MODE=identity_only — only Identity Platform (post T+7)
#
# This is the "1-line swap" REFACTOR-MCP §4.5 talks about — but it's
# wrapped in a feature flag for safety. The flag flips trivially at T+7.
################################################################################
